        worktree `~/work/zen/zenav1-svt--cdef1` on r7900x whose only difference
        from `cand` is `svtav1-dsp/src/cdef.rs`.
cand:   this commit. ONE file: `crates/svtav1-dsp/src/cdef.rs`.
C:      reference/svt-av1 @ 3115c0c1, the PREBUILT oracle in the primary
        r7900x checkout (`rust/tools/perf_c_encode/perf_c_encode`, 2026-09-03),
        NOT rebuilt, passed to the driver as `CE=`.
tools:  Ir — tools/perf_profile/callcount_cells.sh (unchanged), PRESETS=6 QP=40,
        on photo_cid and screen_terminal (CDEF is content-sensitive), both
        512x512, from `r7900x:~/tmp/rc1/yuv`.
        Wall clock — tools/perf_ab.sh, 21 interleaved randomised paired rounds,
        one untimed warmup per sample, NEITHER SIDE NICED.
data:   benchmarks/cdef_i16_kernel_2026-09-05.tsv.

=================== C'S SHAPE, WITH LINE NUMBERS ===================

  ASM_AVX2/cdef_block_avx2.c:1001  svt_cdef_filter_block_avx2   <- the selector
                              :1006   8xn_8_avx2  (BLOCK_8X8, height 8)
                              :1030   8xn_8_avx2  (BLOCK_8X4, height 4)
                              :~1042  4xn_8_avx2  (BLOCK_4X8)
                              :~1054  4xn_8_avx2  (BLOCK_4X4, sub forced to 1
                                      "b/c can't subsample 4x4")
  ASM_AVX2/cdef_block_avx2.c:870   svt_cdef_filter_block_8xn_8_avx2
  ASM_AVX2/cdef_block_avx2.c:713   svt_cdef_filter_block_4xn_8_avx2
  ASM_AVX2/cdef_block_avx2.c:401   constrain16
  Codec/cdef.c:193                 svt_cdef_filter_block_c   <- the port's
                                   `cdef_filter_block_core` is this, verbatim
  Codec/cdef.c:322                 svt_cdef_filter_fb        <- the driver

THE DIFFERENCE, and it is the same CLASS the CfL record found (arithmetic
WIDTH, not linkage): **C keeps the entire filter in i16 lanes and packs
`16 / cols` ROWS into one 256-bit register** — 2 rows x 8 cols in the 8-wide
kernel (`_mm256_setr_m128i` of two `_mm_loadu_si128`, `:902`), 4 rows x 4 cols
in the 4-wide one (`_mm256_set_epi64x` of four 64-bit loads, `:740`). The port
carried the same values in i32 lanes, ONE row at a time: half the lanes, and
`_mm256_mullo_epi32` (`pmulld`, 2 uops on Zen) where C uses
`_mm256_mullo_epi16` (`pmullw`, 1).

A SECOND, INDEPENDENT DIFFERENCE with the same effect: **C groups the taps by
coefficient.** `sum += pri_taps[0] * (p0 + p1)` (`:922`) is ONE multiply for a
PAIR of taps, and `sum += sec_taps[0] * (p0 + p1 + p2 + p3)` (`:958`) one for a
QUAD. Twelve taps therefore cost FOUR multiplies, not twelve. The port
multiplied per tap. That is legal because the port's own scalar core
accumulates `sum` with `wrapping_add::<i16>` and multiplication distributes
over addition mod 2^16 — the grouping is exact, not an approximation.

=================== WHAT LANDED ===================

`cdef_filter_rows_v3::<COLS>` (new, `COLS` = 8 or 4) replaces
`cdef_filter_cols8_v3` for the dst8 arm and covers BOTH column widths. The i32
`cdef_filter_cols8_v3` STAYS — `hbd.rs:1736` uses it for the 10-bit dst16 path,
which is untouched by this commit and not in the 8-bit profile.

`cdef_filter_block_impl_v3` now vector-dispatches on both widths, with a guard
`rows % ((16 / cols) * sub) == 0` (else the scalar core, unchanged). Every
shape the encoder produces passes it: luma is BLOCK_8X8 with
`sub_y = min(cfg.subsampling, 4)` — **4 at preset >= 6** — and 8 % (2*4) == 0;
chroma is BLOCK_4X4 with `sub_uv = min(cfg.subsampling, 1)` = 1 and
4 % (4*1) == 0. The guard exists so an out-of-shape caller mis-strides into the
scalar core rather than silently into the wrong rows.

=================== THREE DELIBERATE DIVERGENCES FROM C'S KERNEL ===================

All three exist to make the vector arm equal `cdef_filter_block_core` (=
`svt_cdef_filter_block_c`) over the WHOLE `&[u16]` input domain. C's own AVX2
kernel disagrees with C's own scalar reference on each of them. **Two of the
three cost nothing; the third costs one instruction per 16 output pixels.**

1. **No `if (pri_strength)` / `if (sec_strength)` tap-group guard.** C skips a
   whole group when its strength is 0, which also skips that group's `min`/`max`
   update; the scalar reference does not. Running the group unconditionally is
   free in `sum` — `constrain16` with `thr == 0` returns 0 in every lane,
   because `_mm256_subs_epu16(0, l) == 0` and the min against it is 0 — and it
   removes a branch.

2. **`_mm256_subs_epi16` + `_mm256_min_epu16` in `constrain16`**, where C uses
   `_mm256_sub_epi16` + `_mm256_min_epi16`. The scalar computes `t - r` in i32,
   exact for the `|diff| <= 65535` an i16 pixel pair can produce; C's i16
   subtract WRAPS there. The saturating form is exact instead, at identical
   cost (both are 1-uop AVX2 instructions): a saturated difference means
   `|diff| >= 32767`, so `|diff| >> shift >= 32767 >> 6 = 511`, which exceeds
   any legal CDEF strength (primary <= 15, secondary <= 4), so
   `subs_epu16(thr, l)` is 0 and the tap contributes 0 — which is exactly what
   the i32 scalar computes there. The UNSIGNED min is what makes the `-32768`
   saturation land on 0 rather than on `-32768`
   (`_mm256_abs_epi16(-32768) == -32768`). Below saturation both instructions
   are bit-identical to their C counterparts.
   **`filter_block_sign_straddle_matches_c` is the test that fails without
   either one** — it feeds pixels that straddle 0x8000 with small gaps,
   precisely the regime where the widths disagree.

3. **`_mm256_and_si256(res, 0xff)` before `_mm256_packus_epi16`.** The scalar
   finishes with `y as u8`, a TRUNCATION; `packus` SATURATES. They differ when
   the clamped result exceeds 255, which happens exactly when the block's
   CENTRE pixel is itself the `CDEF_VERY_LARGE` sentinel: `min == max == x ==
   0x7f7f`, so the scalar writes `0x7f` and a bare `packus` writes `0xff`. The
   encoder never filters a block whose centre is unavailable, so this is
   unreachable from the pipeline — and C's AVX2 kernel has the divergence. One
   `vpand` per 16 output pixels buys exactness. This one was found by the new
   test, not reasoned to: the first version of the kernel used a bare `packus`
   and the test failed on pattern `kind = 2` (all-sentinel).

4. (Same class, no cost) **the sentinel is excluded from `max` by a BLEND**,
   not by C's `andnot(cmpeq(p, large), p)` substitution of zero. Substituting 0
   only matches the scalar's `if p != CDEF_VERY_LARGE { max = max(p, max) }`
   while the running max is non-negative — true of every real pixel, not of the
   whole u16 domain. Same instruction count.

Also: `_mm256_adds_epi16(row, res)` (saturating) for the final add, where the
scalar widens to i32. Exact because the clamp to `[mn, mx]` immediately follows
and `mn <= row <= mx`, so a saturated sum and the true i32 sum clamp equal.

