=================== EXACTNESS ===================

Two new tests, both in `svtav1-dsp/src/cdef.rs`:

  * `cdef_filter_block_simd_matches_scalar_over_the_legal_knob_domain` — the
    knob space EXHAUSTIVELY: all 4 `bsize`s x all 8 directions x all 16 primary
    strengths x all 4 SIGNALLED secondary strengths (mapped through
    `sec + (sec == 3)`, i.e. `{0,1,2,4}`) x dampings 2..=6 (luma
    `3 + (qindex >> 6)` is 3..=6, chroma subtracts 1) x subsampling `{1, 2, 4}`
    — 7,680 knob settings, each on NINE input patterns (flat 0, flat 255,
    all-sentinel, max-contrast checkerboard, a ramp across the entire
    `0..=CDEF_VERY_LARGE` value range, and four pseudorandom 8-bit fills with
    ~1-in-8 sentinels) = **69,120 whole-block comparisons** against
    `cdef_filter_block_core`, driven through the public `incant!` dispatcher so
    every tier the host offers is swept. Inside `for_each_token_permutation`
    with the `PermutationReport` **CONSUMED** (`warnings.is_empty()` and
    `permutations_run >= 2`), so the sweep cannot silently degenerate to the
    native tier. The pixel space is NOT exhaustive and cannot be (12 taps of
    u16); this is stated in the test's own doc comment rather than implied.
  * `i16_sum_accumulator_cannot_overflow_on_the_legal_strength_domain` —
    recomputes the worst-case `|sum|` from the ACTUAL `CDEF_PRI_TAPS` /
    `CDEF_SEC_TAPS` tables and the legal strength ranges (= 228) and asserts
    `sum + 8` stays inside i16, so a future change to either table trips a test
    instead of the bitstream.

POSITIVE CONTROL, run deliberately, not assumed: mutating the kernel's rounding
constant from `+8` to `+9` in the v3 arm ONLY makes
`cdef_filter_block_simd_matches_scalar_over_the_legal_knob_domain` FAIL, and
reverting restores it. (The `& 0xff` divergence above was also caught by this
test before it was reasoned about, which is a second, unplanned control.)

The pre-existing `tests/c_parity_cdef.rs` (11 tests, against real
`libSvtAv1Enc.a`) passes unchanged — including
`filter_block_sign_straddle_matches_c`, which FAILED on the first i16 draft and
is what forced the saturating-subtract / unsigned-min form. **No test was
relaxed, ignored, skipped or rescoped.**

=================== GATES ===================

x86_64 (r7900x, this tree):
  `identity_full_8bit.sh` `IF_TIER=all` **1250 / 1250 byte-identical**
    (+0 pinned, 0 harness errors). The two absent corpora (CID22-photo,
    gb82-photo) are not present on r7900x and the script SAYS SO on stderr;
    1250 is this host's full count, not a silent skip.
  (the remaining x86 gates and the full aarch64 chain are recorded in the
  commit that carries this file — see the message)

=================== MEMORY ===================

Nothing here allocates. The kernel's only state is the caller's `dst` and a
handful of `__m256i` registers; the previous arm's `[i32; 64]` stack scratch
(and the `[i32; 32]` on the 4-wide NEON path) is GONE from the x86 dst8 path,
so the stack frame is smaller, not larger. No heap traffic changed, no buffer
was resized, and the `vec!`/`Box` census of `svtav1-dsp` is untouched.

=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED: C's kernel structure with line numbers, and that the port's
`cols == 4` path had no vector arm at all on x86 (10,752 of 26,816 calls,
62.7 M of 88.7 M Ir); the frame and per-kernel Ir on two contents at p6; the
per-call cost against C's; the wall clock on ten cells at 21 paired rounds each
on a verifiably quiet box; that the vector arm equals the scalar core over the
whole knob domain on nine pixel patterns and over the sign-straddle domain
against real C.

NOT ESTABLISHED: that this closes the CDEF gap — it is still 3.03x C's
instructions per call, and the residual is that C loads 12 taps as 24 128-bit
loads with pointer arithmetic while the port re-derives a `usize` index and
range-checks a slice per tap. Also unmeasured: any preset but 6 for the Ir
(p2/p10), any qp but 40, 10-bit (the dst16 `hbd.rs` arm still runs the i32
`cdef_filter_cols8_v3` and is the obvious next chunk), and the inter arm.

**AND THE OTHER HALF OF THE CDEF ITEM IS NOT TOUCHED BY THIS COMMIT.**
`cdef_find_dir` is now the largest CDEF residual on x86: 17,186,816 Ir over
**8,192 calls** on photo_cid p6 against C's `svt_aom_cdef_find_dir_dual_avx2`
at 851,968 over 2,048 calls-of-2-blocks = 4,096 blocks. That is **20.2x by Ir
and 2x by block count**, and it is TWO independent defects:
  * **No vector arm on x86 at all.** `cdef_find_dir` dispatches
    `incant!(.., [neon, scalar])` — aarch64 has `cdef_dir_partials_neon`,
    x86 has nothing, so it runs the scalar 8x8x8 accumulation at 2,140 Ir a
    block against C's 208.
  * **The apply recomputes what the search already found.** C's
    `svt_av1_cdef_frame` sets `int dirinit = !(use_reference_cdef_fs ||
    use_qp_strength)` (`enc_cdef.c:446`) — i.e. 1 whenever the search ran — and
    `svt_cdef_filter_fb`'s `if (!dirinit || !*dirinit)` (`cdef.c:367`) then
    SKIPS `cdef_find_dir` entirely, reading the per-picture
    `pcs->cdef_dir_data[fbr * nhfb + fbc].dir/.var` the search wrote. The port's
    search caches within itself (`filter_fb_packed`'s `dirinit`,
    `svtav1-encoder/src/cdef.rs:1079`) but `apply_cdef_frame` recomputes at
    `:460`, which is the 4,096 extra calls. Closing it needs the per-fb
    `dir`/`var` carried out of `cdef_search_still` on `CdefPick`, plus C's two
    exceptions (`use_reference_cdef_fs` / `use_qp_strength`, and the SB128
    `dirinit = 0` reset at `enc_cdef.c:449-455`).

