=================== A SECOND WALL-CLOCK PASS, WITH A SAME-BINARY CONTROL ===================

`main@origin ad8da90e` ("the perf_ab bias is the HARNESS, not the box") landed
while this work was in flight and reports that a `perf_ab.sh` control with the
SAME BINARY in both slots reads **1.0043-1.0052** on photo_cid 512² — a
0.4-0.5 % floor against the candidate slot, claimed as intrinsic to the
harness. That would make every number in this record CONSERVATIVE, so it was
worth checking rather than borrowing.

**IT DOES NOT REPRODUCE HERE, and that is a correction to that record's
generalisation.** Run in one session on a verifiably quiet r7900x (uptime
0.02/0.24/0.82 before, 1.03/0.75/0.90 after; `ps -eo pcpu,comm --sort=-pcpu`
top user process 3.2 % plymouthd at both ends; the txt1 lane's `.workongoing`
is a day stale and its process is gone):

    CONTROL, `perf_ab.sh base base`, 21 paired rounds, ident=Y
    photo_cid       512 p2   ratio 0.9996   (0.9970-1.0022)
    photo_cid       512 p6   ratio 0.9992   (0.9971-1.0015)
    screen_terminal 512 p2   ratio 1.0001   (0.9923-1.0017)
    screen_terminal 512 p6   ratio 1.0013   (0.9968-1.0076)

All four straddle 1.0. **The floor for THESE binaries on THIS host is a null**,
so the numbers below are uncorrected. What is established is narrower than
either record alone: a same-binary control is cheap, it is not always zero, and
it must be measured per binary pair rather than assumed from another lane's.

The A/B re-run in the SAME session, immediately after the control, reproduces
the first pass to within 0.001 on every cell — 0.9593 against 0.9590,
0.9819 against 0.9811, 0.9966 against 0.9973, 1.0021 against 1.0024:

    photo_cid       512 p6   0.9593  **1.042x**  (0.9555-0.9618)   [pass 1: 1.043x]
    screen_terminal 512 p6   0.9819  **1.018x**  (0.9764-0.9865)   [pass 1: 1.019x]
    photo_cid       512 p2   0.9966    1.003x    (0.9938-0.9979)   [pass 1: 1.003x]
    screen_terminal 512 p2   1.0021    0.998x    (0.9979-1.0058)   [pass 1: 0.998x]

The two p6 spans sit entirely below 1.0 and entirely below the control's span;
screen_terminal p2 straddles in both passes and stays a NULL.
